[ti:Tea for Two]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]

[00:00.51]Lesson 125 | 第125课
[00:03.46]Tea for two | 两个人的茶
[00:06.26]Listen to the tape then answer this question. | 听录音,然后回答这个问题。
[00:11.22]Does Susan have tea by herself? | 苏珊独自喝茶吗?
[00:16.47]Can't you come in and have tea now, Peter? | 彼得,你不能进来喝茶吗?
[00:20.97]Not yet. | 还不行。
[00:22.38]I must water the garden first. | 我必须先给花园浇水。
[00:25.78]Do you have to water it now? | 你现在必须浇水吗?
[00:29.52]I'm afraid I must. | 恐怕我必须。
[00:31.54]Look at it! | 你看!
[00:33.02]It's terribly dry. | 它干得厉害。
[00:35.41]What a nuisance! | 真讨厌!
[00:38.00]Last summer it was very dry, too. | 去年夏天也很干旱。
[00:41.98]Don't you remember? | 你不记得了吗?
[00:44.16]I had to water it every day. | 我不得不每天都浇水。
[00:47.52]Well, I'll have tea by myself. | 嗯,我要一个人喝茶了。
[00:52.70]That was quick! | 那真快!
[00:54.73]Have you finished already? | 你已经干完了吗?
[00:57.48]Yes. | 是的。
[00:58.64]Look out of the window. | 看看窗外。
[01:01.35]It's raining! | 下雨了!
[01:03.46]That means you don't need to water the garden. | 这意味着你不需要给花园浇水了。
[01:08.80]That was a pleasant surprise. | 那是个惊喜。
[01:12.29]It means I can have tea, instead. | 这意味着我可以喝茶了。